Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 18:23:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] attribution gap-fix (seat-48): re-key the sha-dead provenance
 record + close the license/source-inventory gaps

Fixes G1, G5, G6, G9, G10, G11 of registers/2026-08-29-release-attribution-audit.md. No history rewritten, nothing pushed, no lane-166 branch touched.

G1: native-grandfather.json was keyed to range_base 9ee9fc04c (b10524); the 2026-08-29 base moves (b10524 -> b10636 -> b10680) rewrote every sha and 0 of 289 keys resolved. Re-keyed by exact-subject match against arifi/main: 289/289 unique, 0 ambiguous, 0 unmatched. Prior keys kept per row as sha_pre_rebase. provenance: grandfathered NATIVE 0/476 -> 289/477, FAIL 315 -> 27 (the G2 residue). The rekey_note carries the G12 caveat: the KEY was restored, the fork-authored CLASSIFICATION was NOT re-validated.

G5: licenses/README.md cited 01b3065fe and d40e42fae, both dangling on no branch. Re-pointed to 4c620f3d1 and 19fd8719b, with the dead shas preserved in a note.

G6: sources.json _base_moved_2026_08_29_seat46 cited 0e000710c -> ba14d63d2. The marker-free-TIP measurement is untouched; only the pointer was stale.

G9 CORRECTS THE AUDIT: LICENSE-jsonhpp is not a fork retention with a missing row - it is upstream llama.cpp's own file at the same path on upstream/master, arrived in bd3f59f81, covering vendor/nlohmann/json.hpp. Given a row in a new inherited-from-upstream table so the two retention tables stay derivable from fork takes.

G10: thecodacus-MIT.txt retention row added, naming the public-GitHub fetch source.

G11 SPLITS IN TWO: zuijdwijk is third-party (MIT, retained verbatim as licenses/zuijdwijk-MIT.txt on the ciru precedent); turbomerge is OURS - a local merge workspace in our own src/, authored by hq/m, needing no third-party notice. Both registered in a new sources.json other_remotes block, deliberately NOT in remotes so currency neither fetches nor drift-reports them. DISPOSITION OWED FROM THE PRESIDENT: track or git remote remove.

RESIDUAL HOLE NAMED, NOT CLOSED: retaining zuijdwijk's notice closes the notice obligation, not the unknown-take question. It carries vulkan/strix-halo-port-2, vulkan/qwen4exp-rocmfpx and vulkan/iq3s-mmv-register-spill - our exact work area - and audit D7 proves untrailered takes exist here. No content diff has been run. Owed before publication.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native)
